title: Intro_Screen1
tags: intro cinematic unskippable_first
---
// Black screen. Silence. Then a low heartbeat sound begins.
<<fade_from_black 2>>
<<play_sfx heartbeat_slow>>

// Image: A massive, glorious tree filling the sky — the World Ash in its prime. Glowing. Alive. Cities in its branches.

The World Ash stood for ten thousand years.

Its roots held the earth together. Its branches held the sky.

In its shade, civilizations rose. Kingdoms flourished. The people of Elarion built their lives in its light.

<<wait 3>>
<<play_sfx heartbeat_slow>>
===

title: Intro_Screen2
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image shifts: fire. The tree burning. An army climbing the trunk. The sky cracking.

Then came the Sundering.

An Orc king named Varuuk led his army up the trunk, seeking the power of the gods.

He set the World Ash on fire.

The sky cracked. The branches fell. Every kingdom built in its shade was buried in ash.

<<play_sfx deep_rumble>>
<<wait 3>>
===

title: Intro_Screen3
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: devastation. Ash-covered ruins. Grey sky. Silence.

The people of Elarion lost everything.

Their cities. Their history. Their faith.

The World Ash — the heart of their world — was gone.

<<wait 2>>

Almost.

<<wait 1>>
===

title: Intro_Screen4
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: the last moments. Soldiers falling. Walls breached. Flames everywhere. The enemy is endless.

The enemy was unrelenting. Wave after wave. No end.

The people of Elarion knew they could not survive.

<<wait 2>>

So they made a choice.

<<wait 1>>
===

title: Intro_Screen5
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: people gathering around the base of the dying Ash. Hands on the bark. Golden light flowing from their bodies into the tree. Faces peaceful. Surrendering themselves.
<<play_sfx souls_ascending>>

As the final walls fell, the people of Elarion gave themselves to the tree.

Their souls. Their memories. Their love for the world they built.

Every man, woman, and child pressed their hands to the bark and let go.

They imbued their spirits into the last root of the World Ash.

<<wait 2>>

Not to escape. To wait.

<<wait 1>>

To wait for someone brave enough to bring them back.

<<wait 3>>
===

title: Intro_Screen6
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: the root, now faintly glowing gold. Thousands of tiny lights swirling inside the bark. The sounds of whispers — voices barely audible. A heartbeat.
<<play_sfx heartbeat_growing>>
<<play_sfx whispers_faint>>

The Heartwood holds them still.

Thousands of souls. An entire civilization. Sleeping inside a dying root.

Every faint pulse is a voice. Every glow is a life waiting to be reborn.

They are the Echoes of Elarion.

<<wait 3>>
===

title: Intro_Screen7
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: centuries of neglect. The tree withering. Enemies circling. The glow fading. But not gone.

Centuries passed. The enemies never stopped.

Orcs. Goblins. Elementals. All drawn to the power sleeping in the root.

The Heartwood grew weaker. The whispers grew quieter.

But it never went silent.

<<wait 2>>

It was calling.

<<play_sfx war_drums_distant>>
<<wait 2>>
===

title: Intro_Screen8
tags: intro cinematic
---
// Image: a lone figure approaching. Dawn. The tree pulses — brighter than it has in centuries. The souls stir.
<<play_sfx heartbeat_strong>>

And now — you.

Not a king. Not a chosen one. Just someone who heard the call and came.

The Heartwood recognized you. The souls inside stirred for the first time in a hundred years.

<<wait 1>>

They don't need a savior. They need a defender.

Someone who will stay. Build. Fight. Endure.

Someone who will restore the tree — and in restoring it, set them free.

<<wait 2>>
===

title: Intro_Screen9
tags: intro cinematic final
---
